                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "687193b9-e5e2-3b6f-bafa-2ff9d3b43a11",
                        "entry_id": "b9f1bbb5-7e6d-326c-a6cb-027a3a5962fd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "rodzaj bicza ze splecionych rzemieni"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8a4a04de-17a0-4f2c-990e-cd2528f9787b",
                                "sense_id": "687193b9-e5e2-3b6f-bafa-2ff9d3b43a11",
                                "text": "Uderzył więźnia czarnym knutem przez środek piersi"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3c94c4b-4445-44eb-8c0e-2460952bb656",
                                "sense_id": "687193b9-e5e2-3b6f-bafa-2ff9d3b43a11",
                                "text": "– Wydaje mi się, że do pewnego gatunku ludzi nie dociera dobroć, tolerancja, metody perswazji. Oni potrzebują nad sobą silnego przewodnika z knutem w dłoni"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ab96b815-7892-38a8-aa4b-cbc9eb0d74c6",
                        "entry_id": "b9f1bbb5-7e6d-326c-a6cb-027a3a5962fd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "uderzenie wymierzone knutem (1.1)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fc9df1c8-ed99-4e9a-a1f9-f0d8f6e315fb",
                        "source_entry_id": "b9f1bbb5-7e6d-326c-a6cb-027a3a5962fd",
                        "source_sense_id": "687193b9-e5e2-3b6f-bafa-2ff9d3b43a11",
                        "target_lang_word": "knout",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "knout",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ecdcdcc5-94d0-373d-ab8e-73b1a3e3b5c2",
                                        "entry_id": "02dd981d-be12-3f29-b641-882334eaa886",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A leather scourge (multi-tail whip), in the severe version known as 'great knout' with metal weights on each tongue, notoriously used in imperial Russia."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44bc8b68-b28e-49b0-af61-2ffba1117ba4",
                                                "sense_id": "ecdcdcc5-94d0-373d-ab8e-73b1a3e3b5c2",
                                                "text": "In Moscow, a Court carbonadoes / His ignorant serfs with the knout; / […] / But Eton has crueller terrors / Than these,—in the Windsor Express."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63d70668-2edf-44b3-b810-6ef469b10ac3",
                                                "sense_id": "ecdcdcc5-94d0-373d-ab8e-73b1a3e3b5c2",
                                                "text": "Torture in a public school is as much licensed as the knout in Russia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eaa34152-7262-43f3-8ead-b368cdcb5868",
                                                "sense_id": "ecdcdcc5-94d0-373d-ab8e-73b1a3e3b5c2",
                                                "text": "“I don't suppose a Russian convict under the knout is able to amuse the rest of his gang; and all our men-folk here are gilded convicts.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af97152e-2dc2-4b85-b05a-980a956baf42",
                                                "sense_id": "ecdcdcc5-94d0-373d-ab8e-73b1a3e3b5c2",
                                                "text": "Spray and then slogging knouts of water hit the windows or lights like snarling disaffected at a mansion of the rich and frivolous."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0f4fe63-5588-41a7-bae8-9f9b40a82b99",
                                                "sense_id": "ecdcdcc5-94d0-373d-ab8e-73b1a3e3b5c2",
                                                "text": "The lieutenant gave him twenty strokes of the knout and stuck him in a cage for a few days till the snow was ankle deep."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "knout",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "461a743b-d3c2-3ea3-b7ab-171cb205113e",
                                        "entry_id": "35766105-8dfa-3ee7-a0d2-1e80a249f5c9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To flog or beat with a knout."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0b5fef1-702d-4abf-ac62-11d79bffb0df",
                                                "sense_id": "461a743b-d3c2-3ea3-b7ab-171cb205113e",
                                                "text": "Different, isn’t it? It’s called kava, by the way. The Fijians make it by knouting some root or other."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
